<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid Tank in Cataclysm Classic pre-raid. Gear in this guide is obtained from a multitude of sources including Heroic dungeons, professions, and epic world drops. This guide has been written from a first raid reset point of view and will not be utilizing points of valor points for BiS gear. This will be updated after the first week of raiding is complete.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c11">Best in Slot Gear for Feral Druid Tank in Pre-Raid</span></h2>Feral Druid Tank wants survivability over all other stats. Stamina is king and should be prioritized whenever possible, this means wearing high item level gear and gemming <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52242/solid-ocean-sapphire">
<img alt="Solid Ocean Sapphire" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid Ocean Sapphire</span></a> into most available slots.<ol class="last">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Stamina - This is your most important stat as a Feral Druid Tank. The higher your stamina is the less likely it will be for you to die in a raid environment.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Agility - This is your second best main stat that can be used as a Feral Druid Tank. Agility increases your chance to dodge along with your chance to crit. However, point for point agility is worse than stamina for survivability so it will not be sought after with the use of gem slots.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery Rating/<wbr/>Dodge Rating - Both Mastery and Dodge Rating provide defensive benefits for Feral Druid Tank. Mastery Rating increases the value of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=62600/savage-defense">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_cannibalize.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Savage Defense</span></a> while Dodge Rating decreases the chance that you will be hit. From a survivability standpoint both of these stats are equal, but in any fight where there is <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=57655/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a> uptime mastery becomes a better stat.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike Rating - This provides an increase in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=62600/savage-defense">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_cannibalize.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Savage Defense</span></a> uptime. However this stat is point for point weaker than the other defensive stats.<br/>
<br/>
